@@ -36,6 +36,16 @@ Version 3.3.3 - in development
   `timedelta` so the value carries into the next second instead of overflowing
   the `datetime` microsecond argument. PR submitted by Andrew Chen et AI.
 
+- Fixed `QuotedString` silently discarding white space in its quote characters.
+  `quote_char` and `end_quote_char` were passed through `str.strip()`, so
+  `QuotedString("\n;", multiline=True)` actually parsed strings quoted with just
+  `";"`. White space in the quote strings is now preserved, and any leading white
+  space in `quote_char` is excluded from the expression's whitespace chars, so it
+  is not skipped over while looking for the opening quote. With `multiline=False`,
+  a quoted string still may not span lines, even if the end quote contains a line
+  end. Quote strings that are empty or all white space continue to raise
+  `ValueError`. Issue #492.
+
 - Fixed debug output corruption when a parsed line contains a carriage return or
   other control character. `set_debug()` printed the source line verbatim, so a
   stray `\r` returned the terminal cursor to column 0 and overwrote the "Match ...
